# Every text file in this repo is LF, in the index and in the working tree, on
# every machine. A submodule does NOT inherit the parent repo's .gitattributes,
# so FamCart pinning this for itself did nothing here: a Windows clone has
# core.autocrlf=true, checks these files out as CRLF, and prints a warning per
# touched file.
#
# That is not only noise. scripts/sync-icons.mjs compares the file on disk
# against the upstream package byte for byte (`current === svg`), and the
# upstream copy is LF — so `npm run icons:check` reported three icons as
# drifted on every Windows checkout while the content was identical, and would
# have gone on doing it however many times they were re-synced. A drift guard
# that cries wolf is a drift guard nobody reads.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries, named so text=auto can never misjudge one. Git usually detects
# these on its own; being explicit costs nothing and removes "usually".
*.png binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff2 binary
